# CLU-E Evidence Repository — versioning boundary
#
# Owning contract: CLUE_Git_Integration_v9.md
#   §5.1  two-repository default. This repository is the CLU-E Evidence Repository:
#         "CLU-E code, founding documents, policies, Great Book, status history,
#         small receipts, evidence manifests, and release records".
#   §3    the reference implementation does NOT assume that "large evidence artifacts
#         belong in ordinary Git objects". Bulk evidence is content-addressed and
#         referenced by hash, not committed.
#   §7    the Git State Envelope carries `untracked_manifest_hash` and an optional
#         `ignored_material_manifest_hash`.
#   §7.1  a commit OID does not identify untracked files, generated files used by a
#         benchmark, or sparse-checkout omissions.
#   §8.2  the Git Worktree Pool lives under `workspace/git/worktrees/`.
#
# Why this file must be in-tree and versioned, not in `.git/info/exclude` or a global
# config: §7 hashes the ignored and untracked sets into the Base Pin. A rule that does
# not travel with the commit produces a seal over a set nobody can reconstruct.
#
# Backlog: DEV-P1-09. The predecessor was named `gitignore` — no leading dot — from
# 27 July 2026. Git never read it, so every rule below was inert and 661 MB across
# 2299 paths (node_modules, dist, a 392 MB Navigator stream, a 108 MB SQLite
# projection) was eligible for commit. The rename is the fix; the content below is the
# governance the item also asks for. The predecessor additionally cited
# `CLUE_Strategy_v5.md`, which is not a document in the v9 pack, and enumerated 7 of
# the 21 canonical workspace children — omitting the two largest.
#
# Governing rule, applied below in one direction only:
#   durable truth and small receipts are IN; anything rebuildable from them, and
#   anything bulky, is OUT.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT A RECOVERY IMAGE. The event log is versioned and the artifact
# store is not, and the log references artifacts by hash. A clone therefore carries the
# record of what happened and none of the bytes it points at: `rehydrate` and "the graph
# survives losing the database" both read the artifact store, so neither works from a
# clone alone. That is §3's choice, not a defect — but it is worth saying, because the
# header calls the event log the sole source of truth and a reader may reasonably infer
# that cloning yields recoverable truth.
#
# Artifact bytes come from `workspace/blobs/` on the host and from nowhere else. No
# automated backup path for them is implemented: `config.backup` exists in
# `clue.config.yaml` and in `backupConfigSchema`, but it describes Git ref publication
# for ledger durability, and no module in `src/` reads it. Preserving the artifact store
# is currently a host responsibility with no code behind it.


# --- Build output and toolchain ---------------------------------------------
# Rebuildable from source by `npm ci` and `npx tsc`. `dist/` is also the surface the
# continuation brief warns about: a stale `dist/` reports a meaningless green suite,
# which is a reason to rebuild it, never a reason to commit it.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo


# --- Workspace data plane ----------------------------------------------------
# `src/control/runtime.ts` (WORKSPACE_DIRECTORIES) creates 21 children. Deny all of
# them, then re-include by name. Default-deny is deliberate: a child added later is
# excluded until someone classifies it, rather than silently entering the seal.
#
# Note that a relative `workspace.root` resolves against the installation root
# (`src/control/runtime.ts`), so an in-repository `workspace/` is a supported
# configuration and must be governed here. The shipped `config/clue.config.yaml`
# points at `F:/CLU/workspace/clue`, outside the repository; both cases are covered.
workspace/*

# IN — event log. The append-only sole source of truth (Constitution; Architecture §3).
# SQLite is its derivative, not its authority. Currently 454 KB.
# If rotation is introduced, archives are hash-recorded and this rule needs revisiting.
!workspace/events/
workspace/events/*
!workspace/events/events.ndjson

# IN — Great Book ledger and CLUE_PERFECT / invalidation certificates, bounded to the
# top level of each directory.
#
# Stated honestly: no code writes to either directory yet. Both are created empty by
# `createWorkspaceLayout` and referenced nowhere else in `src/` — the only `ledger`
# hits are a pipeline stage name in `viewModel.ts` and `consoleProjector.ts`, not a
# path. These rules are declared in advance so the first record written is versioned
# rather than lost.
#
# Bounded rather than open because these are the one place where an unwritten
# directory is re-included wholesale: with no writer, nobody has decided what shape
# the contents take, and an unbounded `!` would admit whatever appears first — a run
# directory, a rendered export, a bulk attachment — into the seal without review.
# Records are flat files (`experiments.ndjson`, `GREAT_BOOK_OF_EFFICIENCY.md`,
# certificate and invalidation records), so top-level files are IN and any nested
# subdirectory is OUT until someone classifies it. That is the same default-deny the
# rest of this file uses; it is not a claim that a subdirectory would be wrong.
!workspace/ledger/
workspace/ledger/*/
!workspace/certificates/
workspace/certificates/*/

# OUT, with the reason for each — the four children that actually carry bytes today:
#   workspace/db/       SQLite projections; rebuildable by event replay (108 MB)
#   workspace/graph/    Navigator streams and current pointer (392 MB); DEV-P1-06 owns
#                       their retention and compaction
#   workspace/blobs/    content-addressed artifacts; bulk evidence per §3, referenced
#                       by hash from records that ARE versioned (62 MB)
#   workspace/console/  operational-console.ndjson; a projection of Status, not an
#                       authority (ADR-0002)
#
# OUT — created but not yet written by any code path, so nothing is being discarded:
#   coverage/ documents/ environments/ findings/ implementations/ landings/ logs/
#   patches/ proof-contracts/ runs/ snapshots/ tasks/ temp/ tests/
#
# OUT — Git Worktree Pool (§8.2). Leased experiment worktrees are transient and
# reconstructible from a Base Pin; a nested checkout must never enter this history.
#   workspace/git/worktrees/


# --- Isolation zones outside the workspace -----------------------------------

# Local Configuration-v3 startup selector and byte-exact cutover backups.
/config/project-profiles.yaml
/config/backups/clue.config.v2.*.yaml
# `config/clue.config.yaml` places the shadow clone and the test browser profile
# outside the repository (`F:/CLU/shadow/clue`, `F:/CLU/chrome-profile`). Git cannot
# express an absolute path, and does not need to. These relative rules exist because
# the Linux harness described in the continuation brief §4 builds a temporary
# repository with POSIX roots, where both land inside the tree.
shadow/
chrome-profile/


# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and suspenders. Keys belong in the host secret facility; §5.3 prohibits
# credentials embedded in remote URLs.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem


# --- Release artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
# `npm pack` output. The archive is reproducible from the tagged tree, so the archive
# is out and its checksum manifest is in — DEV-P1-08 owns the release command that
# emits both, and DEV-P1-26 owns the manifest it emits.
*.tgz

# `tools/release.mjs` output: archive, per-file SHA256SUMS, gates log, report. All four
# are regenerable from the tree the report names, and the archive is 2 MB per run. The
# script checks for this rule by name and warns when it is absent, because an unignored
# output directory is how release artifacts end up in the history they describe.
release/


# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store


# --- Tooling residue ---------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
npm-debug.log*


# --- Deliberately NOT ignored, stated so the omission reads as a decision -----
#   PACKAGE_SHA256SUMS.txt      evidence manifest — §5.1 names manifests as IN
#   MANIFEST.txt                release record — §5.1 names release records as IN
#   p0-acceptance-report.json   acceptance receipt, 26 KB — a "small receipt"
#   probe-report.txt            read-only probe receipt, 9 KB — a "small receipt"
#   clue-status.md              status history — §5.1 names status history as IN
#   config/                     governed policy — §5.1 names policies as IN
#   tools/*.mjs, tools/*.js     read-only diagnostics; source, not output
